# mutgap4_sys_iosfc_v1_fourth_component: A v1 plane's fourth component is copied into the v2 form and reaches the IOSurface: one-plane 16x8 BGRA v1 surfaces with four components, the fourth's bit depth 16 (40 bits in 4 bytes), then 200, then 8 with name 0xff and range 0xff, then the good plane (8, name 4), each mapped then tested; each status and data page is locked. Measured: IOSurface validates none of them, and every one maps and tests as the good plane (so how the fourth component is copied does not show here).
{"iosfc": true, "op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
